WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Topographical Anatomy of the Female Pelvic Viscera & Perineum.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The female true pelvis contains the urinary bladder anteriorly, the uterus, uterine tubes and ovaries centrally, and rectum posteriorly.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
The peritoneal reflection between rectum and uterus creates the rectouterine pouch of Douglas, the most dependent part of the female abdominopelvic cavity.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
The broad ligament of the uterus is a double fold of peritoneum extending from the lateral margins of the uterus to the pelvic sidewalls.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:01.000
The pelvic diaphragm (levator ani and coccygeus) forms a dynamic muscular hammock supporting pelvic organs against gravitational descent.
